  "_notes_system_generator": "Star systems generated from a game's seed (game/sim/Space/SystemGenerator.cs; pure, its own hash, not sim.Rng). star: spectral class weights (classes must be in climate/stars.json), radius range and a name list. planets: how many planets and belts (moons come on top), placed one per slot between orbit.min and orbit.max map units (star at 0, 0, like maps.json; slot share jitter keeps neighbouring orbits apart). zones: the band of orbit distances (map units) each zone covers, the au range that band stands for at a Sol-bright star (scaled by the square root of the star's luminosity, so a habitable zone stays habitable round a K or F star; feeds the climate), and the class weights rolled there (any planet_classes id; Class M is the rare roll: 5 of 100 in the habitable zone, none elsewhere); habitable_zone names the zone the landable fallback looks in. belts = classes drawn as rings and named with belt_suffix. moons: how many each parent class gets ([min, max], uniform; absent = none), their class weights by parent class (default for the rest), their distance from the parent and their names (parent name + suffix). sizes: [min, max] per class (default for the rest), the same 1..7 scale as maps.json. names: the planet and belt names, each used once per system. landable_fallback: when no rolled body has a surface (surfaces.json planets), the habitable-zone planet nearest the zone's middle (else the nearest planet that isn't a giant or belt) becomes this class. climate: what each generated body's climate entry gets per class (default for the rest) on top of the class's climate template (climate/classes.json): day_seconds, axial_tilt_deg and eccentricity ranges, albedo, greenhouse_c, spin (prograde share), moons locked to their parent; year_seconds_at_1_au = play seconds of a year at 1 au round a Sol-mass star (Tarsis: 8 days of 720 s), scaled by au^1.5. All numbers are placeholders.",
